    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="3bda5cdc-c1f6-51b6-8705-1337e760a0fc" activityNameId="712ebb90-49fc-55c7-88dc-a12ea7824957" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sewer system, vitrified clay pipe, DN 600, profile 3</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sewer system, vitrified clay pipe, DN 600, profile 3
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 61ebd7ea-510b-4c94-ae6e-d7dc2a641627
This process models deconstruction and end-of-life treatment for 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with vitrified clay pipe. DN 600, profile 3 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for 1 meter of sewer system with vitrified clay pipe, DN 600, profile 3. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 600, profile 3 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Vitrified clay pipe, ID 600 mm, outer diameter 728 mm, wall thickness 64 mm, 267 kg/m, 2000 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_61ebd7ea-510b-4c94-ae6e-d7dc2a641627.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
